  "slug": "microbiome-metagenomics-9f55",
  "summary": "New tools and surveys expose and correct blind spots in microbiome profiling, from missed sludge taxa to eukaryotic bycatch, while host identity structures communities.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is how method choice shapes microbial community interpretation. HiFi long-read metagenomics shows that short-read assemblies of activated sludge miss denitrifiers, nitrifiers and Accumulibacter, biasing N2O-related inferences. RADSuite adds RADlib, a curated 16S rRNA gene copy database, and RADx, which identifies V regions to enable species-level identification. metaEukaryome uses mitochondrial and plastid sequences to detect eukaryotes in 75,727 global metagenomes, revealing cross-domain co-occurrence. Host-associated 16S surveys apply marker-gene profiling: octocoral microbiomes in Florida are stable over three years, driven by host identity and host-specific Endozoicomonas, while Antarctic Haliclystus antarcticus communities vary across gut, peduncle and tentacles, with an antimicrobial gut Oceanisphaera ostreae isolate. The new element is the focus on correcting resolution and taxonomic-scope biases in profiling.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
